Học Tarot — licensing
=====================

This repository holds a built application. Three different things are bundled in
it, under three different terms.


1. Card images — public domain
------------------------------
The 78 card images under `cards/` are scans of the Rider–Waite–Smith tarot deck,
first published in 1909. The deck is in the public domain. The scans were taken
from Wikimedia Commons; the exact source page for each image is recorded in
`cards/sources.json`, and every one reports a public-domain licence.

These are NOT photographs of a modern retail printing. US Games Systems asserts
rights over its own contemporary reproductions of this deck; nothing here comes
from those.


2. Arthur Edward Waite, "The Pictorial Key to the Tarot" (1911) — public domain
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Where the app shows reference text attributed to Waite 1911, that text is in the
public domain and is reproduced verbatim and attributed.


3. Everything else — © 2026 namvh0612, all rights reserved
----------------------------------------------------------
The written card meanings, keywords, the long-form entries, the situation
descriptions, the concept material, and the application code are original work
and are not public domain.

You may download this repository and run the application for your own use. You
may not republish, redistribute, sell, or incorporate the written content into
another work without permission.

If you want to use any of it, ask.


A note on sources
-----------------
The written content was developed with reference to a wide range of published
tarot literature. No prose from any copyrighted modern work is reproduced here.
Where those books were consulted, it was to establish which readings are common
across the tradition and which are one author's idiosyncrasy — facts and ideas,
which are not subject to copyright, expressed in new words.
